      "writtenOn": "2016-11-17T00:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are we sure this is safe? I\u0027m imagining that, once started, gscan keeps running indefinitely. That would mean that the event callback might be executed after startGscan() has returned. In that case, we have a reference to something that may be out of scope.\n\nOr perhaps there\u0027s something I don\u0027t understand about the execution model here...",
      "range": {
