    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7037600d_97390fed",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_legacy_hal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 331,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-11-17T00:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No need for the two step process. Consider a couple of alternatives:\n\n  return {status, std::vector\u003cuint32_t\u003e(freqs.begin(), freqs.begin() + num_freqs)};\nor\n  return {status, {freqs.begin(), freqs.begin() + num_freqs}};\n\nThe first formulation inlines the temporary, instead of having a local, and then asking the compiler to treat that local as a temporary (via std::move()).\n\nThe second pushes a bit further, by nesting the initializer lists.\n\nNote that I\u0027m making this argument entirely on the basis of style (what I think is easiest to read). I suspect that any of the three cases compiles down to the same code (when optimization is enabled).",
      "revId": "3b0b2f8a2b93a8e76663406c27575b4eba76db26",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
